| FSLAm    | 48.74          | 48.74        | 50.88               | 47.24                 | 50.36                 |

================================================================================
EXPERIMENT 1 DETAIL: RUN 1 (v3 Sequential with No ZeroInit)
================================================================================
- CONFIGURATION:
  * Frame-level per-pixel Audio-Visual Spatial Gated Fusion (SGF)
  * Video-level Registry Tokens in VL-AVFM (4 tokens)
  * Frame-level CBAM2D
  * Initialization: Standard random/Xavier weights (No ZeroInit)
  * SGF gate bias init: 0.0 (un-gated / standard init)

- RESULTS & PERFORMANCE:
  * AP: 39.66 (Degraded from baseline 40.23)
  * HOTA: 59.64 (Degraded from baseline 61.11)
  * FSLA: 39.89 (Slightly above baseline, but far below paper)
  * FSLAn: 14.18 (Silent frame accuracy degraded)

- ANALYTICAL DESCRIPTION (WHY):
  Without Zero-Initialization, the newly introduced SGF gating and CBAM modules introduced random, unlearned noise directly into the pre-trained Mask2Former decoder's feature maps at iteration 0. The model was forced to spend a significant portion of its training budget recovering the foundational object detection capabilities rather than refining audio-visual alignment. This resulted in an overall drop in performance across all main metrics.

================================================================================
EXPERIMENT 2 DETAIL: RUN 2 (v3 Sequential with ZeroInit and 3x3 SGF Bottlenecks)
================================================================================
- CONFIGURATION:
  * Frame-level per-pixel SGF (uniform 3x3 bottlenecks on all 3 scales)
  * SGF gate bias init: -5.0 (sigmoid(-5.0) ≈ 0.006)
  * Video-level Registry Tokens (4 tokens)
  * Frame-level CBAM2D with ZeroInit (alpha parameter init to 0.0)

- RESULTS & PERFORMANCE:
  * AP: 41.05 (Exceeded paper by +0.48 and baseline by +0.82)
  * HOTA: 61.64 (Exceeded baseline by +0.53, matching paper performance)
  * FSLA: 41.62 (Exceeded baseline by +2.30)
  * FSLAn: 33.62 (Massive +18.47 improvement over baseline silent frames)
  * FSLAs: 34.45 (Improved small object localization)
  * FSLAm: 47.24 (Degraded medium object localization from baseline 48.74)

- ANALYTICAL DESCRIPTION (WHY):
  * The Zero-Initialization strategy (gate bias of -5.0 and CBAM alpha at 0.0) preserved the pre-trained distribution, allowing the network to build upon the baseline detection capabilities seamlessly, yielding the highest AP (41.05).
  * Registry Tokens successfully provided a "parking lot" to absorb attention mass when audio was uninformative, leading to the massive jump in silent-frame accuracy (FSLAn: 33.62).
  * However, the uniform 3x3 SGF kernel was too large for the 1/16 scale (medium objects), where objects span only a few pixels. This caused excessive spatial boundary suppression (over-gating) and degraded FSLAm.

================================================================================
EXPERIMENT 3 DETAIL: RUN 3 (v3 Sequential with Scale-Specific Kernels and Warmer Bias Init)
================================================================================
- CONFIGURATION:
  * Frame-level scale-specific SGF:
    - Scale 0 (1/8 resolution): 3x3 bottleneck kernel
    - Scale 1 (1/16 resolution): 1x1 kernel (no bottleneck/spatial collapse)
    - Scale 2 (1/32 resolution): 1x1 kernel (no bottleneck/spatial collapse)
  * SGF gate bias init: Warmed to -2.0 (sigmoid(-2.0) ≈ 0.12)
  * Video-level Registry Tokens (4 tokens)
  * Frame-level CBAM2D with ZeroInit (alpha parameter init to 0.0)

- RESULTS & PERFORMANCE:
  * AP: 40.27 (Degraded compared to Run 2)
  * HOTA: 60.23 (Degraded compared to Run 2)
  * FSLA: 40.24 (Degraded compared to Run 2)
  * FSLAn: 0.0 (Complete collapse on silent frames!)
  * FSLAs: 32.64 (Degraded compared to Run 2)
  * FSLAm: 50.36 (Successfully fixed and exceeded baseline 48.74 by +1.62!)

- ANALYTICAL DESCRIPTION (WHY):
  * The 1x1 SGF kernels successfully resolved the over-gating/boundary suppression issue on Scale 1 and 2, which allowed the medium object accuracy (FSLAm) to rise significantly to 50.36.
  * However, warming the SGF bias initialization to -2.0 introduced too much initial audio noise. A 12% feature modification (sigmoid(-2.0)) at iteration 0 meant that even for silent frames (where the VGGish audio vector contains a non-zero silence embedding), the gate injected significant noise into the visual features. The model adapted by assuming every frame had a sounding object, resulting in a catastrophic drop in silent frame accuracy (FSLAn: 0.0) and overall metric degradation.
